    "entrypoint": "61 cases exercise original FileJob::run with owned synthetic inputs. The two-job race calls it twice; one separate unused-job Drop case covers gate lifecycle only. No fake native reports or copied production implementation.",
    "fixtures": "Small in-memory GZip generator uses uncompressed DEFLATE blocks <=65535 and bitwise CRC32. Original content <=65537 bytes, header strings synthetic. No repository/user archive input, shell/network/process launcher or host font access.",
    "coverage": {
        "normal": "Empty/one/known bytes and 65535/65536/65537 outputs; actual published bytes, observed input identity/SHA256, GZip boundary/CRC, file receipt identity, native durability, close results and namespace.",
        "ownership": "Replace owned input pathname only at Decode::Start after snapshot completed. Output still comes from old captured bytes; replacement and saved original remain intact until assertions finish. Header FNAME/FCOMMENT are not destinations.",
        "invalid": "Bad magic, invalid DEFLATE, CRC/ISIZE mismatch, concatenated member, trailing byte and truncated trailer retain typed error class; publication events/Usage remain zero and output absent.",
        "usage": "Exact small-input budgets and one-less snapshot bytes/I/O/read calls, GZip input/processed/output/metadata and publication bytes/I/O/calls. Invalid zero durations at each stage. Compare final counters including post-checkpoint decode charge; no sums across incompatible units.",
        "observer": "Rc pointer-identical non-Send callback errors at snapshot Finalizing, decode AfterOutput and publication BeforeCommit survive an overlapping accepted cancellation. Later stage events/output forbidden.",
        "cancellation": "Pre-request idempotence; first checkpoint at all 5 snapshot, 7 decoder and 4 publication stages; local Stop::Cancelled at each phase; external acknowledged BeforeCommit cancellation; Finished after return preserves committed bytes.",
        "namespace": "Existing file/directory/symlink and input==output retain bytes/identity; owned parent rename at BeforeCommit still commits to pinned old parent. Two prepared FileJobs compete for one name with exactly one full winner and one typed EEXIST.",
        "cleanup": "No Drop cleanup for Sandbox. Assertions and bounded thread completion precede explicit finish; failed files stay for diagnosis. Check owned open descriptors before removing only identity-matched private case root.",
        "reports": "Actual NotCommitted/Committed exercised with native Cleanup and durability. CommitUncertain, failed sync/close are not fabricated as execution evidence."
    },
    "unverified": [
        "Rust type checking, compilation, discovery and runtime of these new tests are deferred until fixed head review.",
        "TooLate CAS-to-link window has no deterministic barrier. Finished after return is not TooLate coverage.",
        "Non-EEXIST linkat/CommitUncertain, file or parent fsync failures, close failures, partial/zero writes, read/seek errors, allocation failures and adverse filesystem faults are not deterministically injected.",
        "MissingSelectedOutput and SelectedLengthMismatch cannot be produced by the normal decoder API. No private receipt construction or syscall interposition.",
        "Real elapsed deadline expiry, hostile concurrent input ABA, crash durability, physical deletion and hard resource interruption are unverified.",
        "OS worker isolation, product Published, UI integration, Windows, Ubuntu24 native platform and folder extraction are outside this suite.",
        "Prior PR51 54 passes are native publication evidence only and are not counted as FileJob executions."
    ],
    "minimum_seams": "Only if separately requested: test-only syscall-result injection and post-CAS barrier owned by backend, plus private selected-output validation helper. No public receipt constructor; no production modification in this candidate.",
    "review": "Fixed control flow preserves snapshot failure usage, final GZip Budget even after last checkpoint, original publication report and accepted cancellation gate. No confirmed source defect from read-only review; static review is not runtime proof.",
